hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-15 = unlines (cons "What the norm, the carpenter's square turned on minds, erases, the old words protect. *Health* is Old English *hælþ*, from *hāl*, whole: the root of *whole*, *hale*, *heal* and *holy*. Health is wholeness, not normality. *Safe* is Latin *salvus*, also whole, from a root shared with Greek *holos*. So the double meaning of *safe* across secure systems and aligned systems has a third layer underneath both: safety is wholeness. A safe system is one that is not split. An aligned agent is one whose action is whole with the person it acts for. A healthy mind is a whole mind, however far it turns from the carpenter's square." nil)
